{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_607a9dbacfcca7a49dcae274c51d1466c5b54980d70adbe6f84bcd5c5bfb4eba"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The FAQ notes that any package an LLM agent tries to use must already be installed in the running virtualenv; self-created per-generation virtualenvs are planned on the roadmap."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8d4640ef4d158be0a6db3a7228998a3d82993e21701395b55e21bda0e0e0b5cf"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors join the dev team by submitting a PR, with ongoing tasks listed on the roadmap; a rotating Chief Evangelist community role is recruited via email."}],"claim_ids":["clm_607a9dbacfcca7a49dcae274c51d1466c5b54980d70adbe6f84bcd5c5bfb4eba","clm_8d4640ef4d158be0a6db3a7228998a3d82993e21701395b55e21bda0e0e0b5cf"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:39:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_528de8705e784752be8205edc0189def","id":"pg_21266c5e897d550b838c91db67a2343d","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/samholt-l2mac-docs-guide-faq-md-105e74afdc67-91db67a2343d.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_49df1e30bf5757a4a3b97f525fdd4e75"],"title":"samholt/L2MAC/docs/guide/faq.md @ 105e74afdc67","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:39:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_528de8705e784752be8205edc0189def"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_38802e992c323b0c3772365c82c4d3c5228e8cd06ee342b87af5f840288c35e3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tools_enabled parameter controls which functions agents can use, defaulting to all available tools; for codebase generation, tools include syntax-error checking and running unit tests."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4f6790d79109c2af1a8e29c7601bd75a44033d73a294658db5e635ad3c6277d3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"L2MAC reads and updates existing code files created many instruction steps earlier, and generates unit tests used as an error checker to fix code that fails after updates."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6e34f0918824d10bbc18e4c655bb9a8208177c37650d5d8786fc358697c5f903"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Each prompt-program instruction step is loaded into a new LLM agent whose context is managed by a control unit and given tools to read and write a persistent file-store holding final and intermediate outputs."},{"claim_ids":["clm_892b17f9d243d77fbdda0a3b6d2293d1a1a02a44f375bb4b550d21a41e0ecb6c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README reports benchmark results: the highest percentage of implemented user-specified features on system design tasks (averaged over 10 random seeds) and a claimed 90.2% Pass@1 on HumanEval."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9898baa4293b785f998b047fd9e75ac557663249290b5c00743af2b494cdeb29"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The prompt-program is a sequence of instruction-step prompts; unless explicitly given, it is self-generated (bootstrapped) and then executed."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a04e8c4b1684de0695edef34e3e9c971362ac1e985cbd39229659a81c88738c6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"L2MAC is described as an LLM-based multi-agent system implementing a stored-program von Neumann-style architecture for extensive, consistent output generation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a3587c5c5ca174845d6e4cafea96026f314e4869f60627c583f8ac65ba34533d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"L2MAC offers a CLI (e.g. `l2mac \"...\"` creating a codebase repo in ./workspace) and a Python library API including generate_codebase and run_l2mac, plus helper functions for book and custom domains."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c05feff024bc3d2c437852991ede8b9984b4c6fdcb23a233fda5af8e4249f7d1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration uses an LLM API with api_type (e.g. openai or azure), model (example gpt-4o), base_url, and api_key, set in ~/.l2mac/config.yaml or initialized via `l2mac --init-config`."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d750e279a85365211b4d8f2c3bd325f1ce1a2be42ccb7267d5260fd70db0f13a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The framework aims to produce outputs unbounded by the underlying LLM's fixed context window by persisting outputs to a file store."},{"claim_ids":["clm_edd71fb9fc6c8aaf4c6e591bb5ca20930f2faf275be81c0a8ef9f7045a006c50"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"requirements.txt lists pyyaml, pydantic, typer>=0.9.0, numpy, openai, tiktoken, timeout-decorator, and pygame==2.1.2; the README states Python 3.7+ is needed."}],"claim_ids":["clm_38802e992c323b0c3772365c82c4d3c5228e8cd06ee342b87af5f840288c35e3","clm_4f6790d79109c2af1a8e29c7601bd75a44033d73a294658db5e635ad3c6277d3","clm_6e34f0918824d10bbc18e4c655bb9a8208177c37650d5d8786fc358697c5f903","clm_892b17f9d243d77fbdda0a3b6d2293d1a1a02a44f375bb4b550d21a41e0ecb6c","clm_9898baa4293b785f998b047fd9e75ac557663249290b5c00743af2b494cdeb29","clm_a04e8c4b1684de0695edef34e3e9c971362ac1e985cbd39229659a81c88738c6","clm_a3587c5c5ca174845d6e4cafea96026f314e4869f60627c583f8ac65ba34533d","clm_c05feff024bc3d2c437852991ede8b9984b4c6fdcb23a233fda5af8e4249f7d1","clm_d750e279a85365211b4d8f2c3bd325f1ce1a2be42ccb7267d5260fd70db0f13a","clm_edd71fb9fc6c8aaf4c6e591bb5ca20930f2faf275be81c0a8ef9f7045a006c50"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:39:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_528de8705e784752be8205edc0189def","id":"pg_2711b60da26451ec99355fd022a1e9ae","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/samholt-l2mac-readme-md-105e74afdc67-5fd022a1e9ae.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_bf415efb5e1055d583ada98510945b8a"],"title":"samholt/L2MAC/README.md @ 105e74afdc67","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:39:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_528de8705e784752be8205edc0189def"}
